\title{nosZviz: Publication-Ready Visualization of NosZRef nosZ Profiling Results}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A comprehensive, one-stop visualization toolkit designed specifically for the output directory of the NosZRef pipeline (\url{https://github.com/ZhangBaoshan668/NosZRef}). It parses every intermediate and merged result file produced by NosZRef (branch-level RPKM and read counts, OTU tables, rarefied tables, seven-rank taxonomic profiles, alpha diversity indices, rarefaction curves, beta diversity distance matrices, and co-occurrence network topology) and turns them into more than sixty publication-quality figures covering gene abundance partitioning, taxonomic composition, alpha diversity, beta diversity ordination, differential abundance, network topology, and - new in 0.2.0 - a clade-ecology narrative layer: clade-resolved nested composition, clade II/I abundance ratios, LEfSe-style and indicator-taxa analyses, taxa dendrograms, and environmental association figures (RDA/CCA/db-RDA, envfit, alpha-environment correlation, taxa-environment networks) together with a one-click HTML/PDF report.

The package reads the complete output directory of the NosZRef pipeline
and provides a coherent grammar of graphics for nosZ-I / nosZ-II / nosZ-III
profiling: gene abundance partitioning, taxonomic composition, alpha and
beta diversity, differential abundance and co-occurrence networks.
}
